    sections: [
      {
        id: 's1',
        title: '1. Introduction',
        content: `
          <p><strong>Dr. Fix</strong> is an intelligent assistant specialized in diagnosing mechanical, electrical, and industrial faults in technical equipment and devices. The app analyzes fault descriptions and user-provided data to generate AI-powered diagnostic suggestions, alongside preventative maintenance guidance and a specialized technical community.</p>
          <p>We are committed to protecting our users' privacy. This policy precisely describes what data the app collects, how it is used, and with whom it may be shared.</p>
        `
      },
      {
        id: 's2',
        title: '2. Data We Collect',
        content: `
          <h3>a. Diagnostic Input Data</h3>
          <p>When using the diagnostic feature, the app requests the following:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Device name</strong>, type, and model (entered manually by the user).</li>
            <li><strong>Fault description and technical notes</strong> (text entered by the user).</li>
            <li><strong>Optional photos</strong> of the device or fault (chosen by the user from camera or gallery — no photo is ever sent automatically without explicit user selection).</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>b. Account Data (Registered Users Only)</h3>
          <p>If the user chooses to sign in with a Google account:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Email address</strong> linked to the Google account.</li>
            <li><strong>Name</strong> as displayed on the Google account.</li>
            <li><strong>Profile photo</strong> from the Google account (if available).</li>
          </ul>
          <blockquote>Users who choose Guest Mode do not have any data from their device uploaded to the cloud.</blockquote>
          <h3>c. Diagnostic History</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Diagnostic results are saved locally on the device.</li>
            <li>For registered users: history is also saved in an encrypted cloud database to enable access from multiple devices.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>d. Location</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>The app requests <strong>approximate location</strong> permission to determine the local currency for displaying spare part costs and nearby service companies.</li>
            <li>Location data is not stored or shared with any external party.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>e. Community Content (Optional)</h3>
          <p>When sharing a case in the expert community:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Fault description and solution</strong> entered by the user.</li>
            <li><strong>Name and specialty</strong> (optional — posting anonymously is supported).</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>f. Technical Identifiers</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Device Technical Token (FCM Token)</strong>: Generated for technical support and customer service purposes only. It is not used for tracking or advertising.</li>
          </ul>
        `
      },
      {
        id: 's3',
        title: '3. How We Use Your Data',
